== library | MORNING · LIBRARY | bright library with study tables and English textbooks | cafe
tomy (worried): Quddus, English is our official language. Why do they want me to pay for an English test?
quddus (talk): Many universities ask international students for proof of English. But the rules are different for every program.
tomy (think): IELTS, TOEFL, Duolingo... it sounds like a boy band.
quddus (talk): Ha! Those are common tests. Some universities accept all of them. Some accept only one or two.
> 1f4ac | ENGLISH PROOF | 1f4dd IELTS or TOEFL: widely accepted | 1f4bb Duolingo English Test: some schools | 1f393 Waiver: some, if your degree was in English

== room | EVENING · TOMY'S ROOM | cozy bedroom at evening with books and a laptop on a desk | phone
tomy (think): So how do I know which one to take?
quddus (point): Check the admission requirements page of each program. Look for the exact test, and the minimum score.
tomy (talk): And this waiver thing?
quddus (talk): Some programs waive the test if your degree was taught in English. You may need a letter from your university. Email admissions and ask.
tomy (cheer): Step one: check. Step two: email. Step three: maybe save my test money!
